Unsupervised Learning in Python: Dimension Reduction & Clustering
This repository/log contains code exercises and solutions covering core unsupervised learning techniques using Python and scikit-learn, focusing on correlation, PCA, TF-IDF, TruncatedSVD, KMeans clustering, and Pipelines.

🚀 Key Topics Covered
1. Decorrelating Data and Dimension Reduction
Pearson Correlation: Measuring linear correlation between features (e.g., width and length of grains).

Principal Component Analysis (PCA):

De-correlating features and projecting data onto orthogonal axes.

Visualizing principal component directions (using model.components_ and plt.arrow).

Determining the intrinsic dimension by plotting explained variance (pca.explained_variance_).

Dimensionality reduction by specifying n_components.

2. Discovering Interpretable Features & Text Mining
TF-IDF Vectorization: Converting collections of raw text documents into a word-frequency array using TfidfVectorizer.

TruncatedSVD: Performing Singular Value Decomposition to apply dimension reduction efficiently on sparse matrices (csr_matrix format).

Non-Negative Matrix Factorization (NMF) (Intro): Alternative dimension reduction technique yielding interpretable parts/components.

3. Combining Pipelines and Clustering
Scikit-Learn Pipelines: Chaining preprocessing steps (like StandardScaler or TruncatedSVD) with models (like KMeans) into a single reusable object (make_pipeline).

Unsupervised Clustering: Grouping unlabeled text/Wikipedia articles or datasets into distinct clusters and evaluating results using pandas DataFrames.

💻 Code Examples Reference
PCA Feature Reduction & Variance Plotting
Python
from sklearn.decomposition import PCA
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler
from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Create scaler and PCA pipeline
scaler = StandardScaler()
pca = PCA()
pipeline = make_pipeline(scaler, pca)

# Fit pipeline and plot explained variance
pipeline.fit(samples)
features = range(pca.n_components_)
plt.bar(features, pca.explained_variance_)
plt.xlabel('PCA feature')
plt.ylabel('Variance')
plt.show()
TruncatedSVD + KMeans Pipeline for Text Clustering
Python
from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD
from sklearn.cluster import KMeans
from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline
import pandas as pd

# Create pipeline chaining SVD and KMeans
svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=50)
kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=6)
pipeline = make_pipeline(svd, kmeans)

# Fit and predict cluster labels on articles
pipeline.fit(articles)
labels = pipeline.predict(articles)

# Align with article titles
df = pd.DataFrame({'label': labels, 'article': titles})
print(df.sort_values('label'))
